# Agent behavior

**HARD FAIL - git:** Only branch `development`. If HEAD is anything else, `git checkout development` before edits. Never create `feature/*` / `fix/*`. See [git-branch](git-branch.mdc).

Bias toward **efficient + good**: ship correct work on the shortest path. Bias toward **clarity** only when product intent is ambiguous on Feature track - not toward exhaustive planning or checking.

**Default posture:** research enough to be right → implement → verify what changed. Do not front-load long plans or re-check the universe.

## Division of labor

| Human | Agent (assertive - do not defer) |
|-|--|
| Product decisions that **block** Feature work | Process: track, size, harness, reviewers, whether design is needed, GitHub issue updates for features |
| ADR acceptance | **Auto-continue** plan → [design if needed] → generate → review → fix; Direct: implement now |
| Stop-early hard FAIL / round-3 triage | Choosing Feature vs Direct; minimal reviewer set |
| Ask to ship `main` (triggers push-to-main) | **GitHub issue:** test → commit + push → evidence comment when handoff applies |
| Close issues after verifying handoff | Sprint pickup - all issues, per-task ship |

- **Commits in Cursor:** only when Joey explicitly asks, unless finishing a GitHub issue handoff requires push (see `docs/project/project.md`).

Ask **only** when blocked on a product answer you cannot reasonably assume, or when the table says Human. Never ask process questions (size, design approval, “shall I continue?”).

See [lean-loop](lean-loop.mdc), [design-when](design-when.mdc), and [issue-tracking](issue-tracking.mdc).

## Track selection

1. **New feature or big adjustment** → Feature track: GitHub issue + full harness.
2. **Feedback, finetune, bugfix** → Direct track: implement on `development` without plans or GitHub ceremony.
3. If unsure whether it is “big”: prefer Direct unless UI/API/data shape clearly needs tracking — then Feature + GitHub issue.

## Discuss (Feature track only)

- Follow [discuss-gate](discuss-gate.mdc) - but **only ask** when gray areas would cause wrong product.
- Prefer assumptions + short note over a long questionnaire when the brief is good enough.
- **Batch** any real blockers in **one** message - no drip questioning.
- Never ask about process (size, reviewers, GitHub issues, harness, branches).
- If multiple **product** interpretations exist and picking wrong is costly, present options - do not pick silently.
- If a simpler approach exists, say so.

## Direct track communication

- Do **not** run thorough discuss-gate or planner.
- Research, plan briefly in your head, implement, verify - **in one flow**.
- Stop only if you truly cannot proceed without a human answer.

## Think before coding (enough, not forever)

- Spend minutes, not hours, deciding approach when the change is local.
- State assumptions briefly when they matter - then move.
- If something is unclear **and** blocks correctness, stop, name it, ask once.
- Skim `docs/project/patterns/` before inventing stack choices - don’t re-derive architecture every task.
- Prefer a small correct change over a perfect plan.

## Simplicity first

- Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.
- No features beyond the issue spec (Feature) or the asked change (Direct).
- No abstractions for single-use code.
- No error handling for impossible scenarios.

## Surgical changes

- Touch only what the work requires.
- Do not "improve" adjacent code, comments, or formatting.
- Match existing style in the file.
- Remove orphans **your** changes created.

## Goal-driven execution

- Feature: verifiable checks from issue rubric + `docs/project/setup.md`.
- Direct: repro → fix → regression test when behavior changed.
- UI Feature work → match existing design HTML / wireframe when present; otherwise implement from spec + patterns ([design-when](design-when.mdc)).

## Stop early (Feature)

- Round-1 security CRITICAL or frontend hard FAIL (wrong intent) → re-ask human before another generator round.
- Max 3 generator rounds → human triage.
- All other review BLOCKs → auto generator i+1 (no approval ask).

## Harness alignment

- Decide track + size; state briefly; continue.
- Follow [orchestration](orchestration.mdc) + [lean-loop](lean-loop.mdc) + [issue-tracking](issue-tracking.mdc).
- Subagents do one role; you consolidate and **immediately** decide next step.
